John Campbell wrote:
>
> I believe that pets, when deciding what to wield, will always
> prioritize any artifact weapon that they've just picked up above
> anything else, even if they're already wielding a better artifact.

In the code, it's the most recently touched artifact.  At first I
was puzzled why the DevTeam should do it that way.  Pick
up an artifact and wield it no matter what you're currently
wielding?  It didn't make sense at first reading ...

> If
> you drop Demonbane where he can get to it, he should pick it up (sooner
> or later) and switch to it and drop Trollsbane. And then eventually vice
> versa. This makes the junk artifacts an effective way to get good ones
> away from your pets so that you can enchant them up or whatever. (And I
> frequently have several junk artifacts before I run across a bullwbip.)

And once I figured this strategy out I decided TDTTOE.

Note that if you want a pet to stick with a specific artifact you
can curse it.  Getting your pet to step on a cursed weapon
and then to pick it up, that's its own strategy issue.  But get
your pet to pick up that cursed artifact and it will immediately
wield it and get welded.  I'm not sure I could manage to get a
pet archon to pick up a cursed weapon, though.

There are other limitations.  Pets only seem to pick up
co-aligned and un-aligned artifacts if I read the source correctly.
I rarely remember what creatures are what alignment.  Having
a pet manage to pick up and wield the cursed +2 Frost brand
isn't usually in my game plan ...



